> was taken from my credit, returned to get the rest of the money (no tip
> intended :-), but the shopkeeper demanded to be the owner of all the
> 2574 pieces of gold that was lying on the floor. (This bastard; I knew
> why I gave no tip!)

Can't be bothered to test it right now, but the way it works IIRC is
that the gold on the floor indeed becomes the shopkeeper's property as
soon as you drop it -- but the shopkeeper then owes you the same
amount of zorkmids.

When you teleport away with something unpaid, the whole physical pile
of gold still belongs to the shopkeeper, _and_ their debt to you is
reduced by the price of the items you took.  Thus, you can no longer
just walk in, pick up the entire pile of gold and expect to just walk
out with all of it.

What you should be able to do is pick up the gold, get the message
that you now owe the shopkeeper some amount of zorkmids, and drop only
that many zorkmids to settle the debt.  Or, if you want to be careful,
chat with the shopkeeper before picking up the gold to find out how
much credit you have left, and only pick up that many gold pieces in
the first place.  (Tip: remove $ from pickup_types.)

Or just get a pet to steal the pile of gold from the shop.

